.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 524 AM PDT Thu Aug 13 2026

The upper level low continues to pull high level clouds over the
region, while the marine layer deepens and spreads stratus.
Terminals generally sit within the MVFR cig territory this morning
and should hold. A few models show some IFR potential for North Bay
terminals, but confidence is moderate to low for that. Any stratus
that has formed is expected to erode or retreat to the coast by mid
to late morning, with high clouds lingering. Breezy onshore winds
return this afternoon and into the evening, where we could see
sustained speeds between 10-15 kt with gusts to 15-25kt. Stratus
returns tonight, likely onsetting between 01Z-09Z. The later start
times favor interior Bay Area terminals.

 Vicinity of SFO...The stratus made it to SFO tonight bringing MVFR
cigs with it. Models differ on how long the stratus holds, with the
times ranging from 14-16Z. A few low clouds may linger throughout
the day, with stratus returning tonight due to the deepening marine
layer. Breezy onshore winds, with gusts up to 25kt possible, return
mid to late afternoon and continue until sunset.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Cigs have been improving tonight, with the
latest METARs showing MVFR cigs around 1500-2500ft. Look for this to
continue through the rest of the morning hours, with skies clearing
by mid to late morning. Onshore flow picks up and should remain a
bit breezy through sunset. Stratus returns early, and will likely
fall to MVFR between 01-03Z with IFR cigs being possible after 06Z.

